# The timing record's artifact upload fails when there is no record (#529)

`CONTRIBUTING.md` ENV-03 says a run that leaves no timing record fails its job
rather than uploading an empty artifact.  The seven workflow steps that upload
`.timings/` carry `if-no-files-found: warn`; this patch makes each one `error`.
A missing record is then a red job, which is what "every run leaves one" has to
mean on the workflow side: an artifact that is empty is indistinguishable from a
run whose `.timings/` was never written.

**Install (one command, from the repository root):**

```sh
git apply results/issue529-upload-error.patch
```

Then commit the seven modified workflows.  They are
`coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml`, `coble-kernel-plane-rows.yml`,
`enriques-polarization-rows.yml`, `isotropic-reduction-image-tests.yml`,
`readme.yml`, `research-388-acceptance.yml` and `research-564-sage-image.yml` —
the seven whose jobs this repository defines, all of them changed in one line
each.  `development.yml` and `ambient.yml` are `uses:` calls to `ai-review-ci`'s
reusable `_qc.yml`, which owns every step and takes no artifact path, so their
record is that workflow's to upload.

The patch is the diff against `5d408ca` (where commit `34b52a8` put the steps),
and it is a file rather than history because the connection that pushed this
work may not update a file under `.github/workflows/`: GitHub refuses such a ref
with "refusing to allow a GitHub App to create or update workflow ... without
`workflows` permission", which is a permission of the App behind the connection.
diff --git a/.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml b/.github/workflows/coble-gamma-co-2-incidence-rows.yml
index 9e718dd..cfeab5a 100644
